# Keep fm350-radio's persistent state across a settings-preserving sysupgrade, and include it
# in `sysupgrade -b` / LuCI "Generate archive" backups.
#
# Named files rather than the whole /etc/h5000m/ directory: h5000m-sms-archive already claims
# the directory form, and two packages shipping the same keep.d path would collide.
#
# Why these must survive an upgrade, not just a reboot: the modem's own band/RAT selection and
# cell lock are stored in the MODEM, and were measured to survive both a reboot and a full
# sysupgrade - the manual's "Persistent: No" for AT+GTACT is wrong. So the radio comes back
# from an upgrade still narrowed, and if the record of what it was BEFORE the lock did not come
# back with it, unlock has nothing to restore and silently leaves the radio pinned to LTE.
/etc/h5000m/fm350-radio.prevact
/etc/h5000m/simslot.pending
# The dialer's reboot guard bounds how many times a stuck bearer may reboot the router. A
# sysupgrade that reset it to zero would hand a still-broken link a fresh budget of reboots,
# so it has to survive the upgrade too. One file per interface (glob).
/etc/h5000m/fm350-*.reboot-guard
